# Cray's men at the pier end, unloading kelp.
dialogue weather4
  node root weather "Evening, sir. We're unloading. Nothing to see. It's kelp."
    > "What's the kelp for?" if not seen:weather4.for -> for
    > "Aren't you meant to be menacing me?" if not seen:weather4.menace -> menace
    > "Who signs for it?" if not seen:weather4.signs -> signs
    > "I've seen kelp crates like those before. On the Marrow." if kelp_seen and not seen:weather4.marrow -> marrow
    > "Goodnight." -> bye
  node for weather "Fog—"
    -> fires
  node fires weather2 "Fires! It's for fires, sir. Fog's just what fires do if you're not careful. We're very careful."
  node menace weather "Not my turn, sir. It's Bartle's turn."
    -> tuesday
  node tuesday weather2 "I did Tuesday. I did all last week. My voice is shot from menacing. You do him."
    -> argue
  node argue narrator "They argue about it, politely, with their backs to the crates. Nobody menaces me at all."
  node signs weather "Mr Cray, sir. Everything's signed for. There's a manifest on the crate, if you're customs. You're not customs?"
    -> customs
  node customs weather2 "He's got a stamp, Wilf."
    -> dont
  node dont weather "Then don't look at it too hard, sir. It's only kelp. It's shy."
  node marrow weather "The Marrow? Can't be, sir. Them crates were for the station. Station's shut, they tell us. Nobody's told the kelp."
  node bye weather "Goodnight, sir. Mind the fog."
    -> nofog
  node nofog weather2 "There isn't any fog."
    -> anyway
  node anyway weather "Mind it anyway."
